Issue_Captable_Unit_Concrete_Test
├── when the caller is neither the Safe nor a module with an issuer allowance
│   └── it should revert with OnlyBoard
├── when the class does not exist
│   └── it should revert with UnknownClass
├── when the amount is 0
│   └── it should revert with ZeroAmount
├── when the Captable is closed for an exit
│   └── it should revert with CaptableClosed
├── when the class votes and a company proposal is pending
│   ├── when the time is at or before the Governor's pendingUntil
│   │   └── it should revert with ProposalPending with the class and the time
│   └── when the time is after pendingUntil
│       └── it should issue and leave the shares out of that vote
├── when the class has a class Governor with a proposal pending
│   └── it should revert with ProposalPending
├── given the class has weight 0 and a company proposal is pending
│   └── it should issue
└── when the caller may issue now
    ├── when a module's allowance is less than the amount
    │   └── it should revert with IssuerAllowanceExceeded
    ├── when issued plus convertible reserve plus the amount is more than authorised
    │   └── it should revert with AuthorisedExceeded
    └── when it fits
        ├── given the caller is a module
        │   └── it should lower its allowance by the amount
        ├── it should mint the shares to the receiver
        ├── given the receiver never held this class
        │   └── it should delegate the receiver's votes to themselves
        ├── given the receiver is the Safe
        │   └── it should mint the shares with no votes and keep them out of supply
        ├── given the class is frozen
        │   └── it should still issue
        └── it should emit Issued with the reason
